{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said.</b> It would have been fitting for the passage of \"and Moses said, thus says HaShem\" to be joined to this verse, and between them would enter the passage of \"one plague more.\" The reason is to indicate that which is said, \"thus says HaShem\" — and when was it said to him? This was said to him in Midian: \"Behold, I will slay your son, your firstborn\" (Exodus 4:23). And with the coming of the plague of the firstborn, He commanded by HaShem at Mount Sinai that they should ask, each man of his fellow. I have already explained why there it is written ושאלה אשה משכנתה (a woman shall ask of her neighbor) (Exodus 3:22), while here it is written וישאלו איש מאת רעהו (they shall ask, each man of his fellow). And so its meaning is: and HaShem said to Moses, one plague more — and HaShem had already said this to Moses, for instances are many — ויאמר גרש יגרש, as He said, \"and with a strong hand he shall drive them from his land\" (Exodus 6:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved the citation 'וביד חזקה יגרשם מארצו (ו א)' to Exodus 6:1, though the phrasing differs slightly from the standard verse text."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:22.194886322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}